From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: file: URLs read from their AmigaDOS paths

The port's file loader (ResourceHandle::amigaLoadFile, 0002) read
url.fileSystemPath(), the URL's path with its leading "/". AmigaDOS
reads a leading "/" as the parent directory, so file:///DH1:dir/page.html
and file:///Work/page.html were "The file does not exist." in the GUI.

The path now goes to AmigaDOS form first:
- file:///Volume:dir/file (PROGDIR:, any assign) is Volume:dir/file;
- file:///Volume/dir/file is Volume:dir/file;
- one name (file:///page.html, the base of a page loaded from memory)
  stays relative to the current directory;
- dir/file that exists relative to the current directory is read there
  before it is taken as Volume/file. The check is relative, so a missing
  volume never brings up an "insert volume" requester.
The MIME type is taken from the same path.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/ResourceHandleAmiga.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/ResourceHandleAmiga.cpp
index 8461ff0..c402dc1 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/ResourceHandleAmiga.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/ResourceHandleAmiga.cpp
@@ -200,6 +200,32 @@ void ResourceHandle::amigaStartCurlRequest(ResourceRequest&& request)
     d->m_curlRequest->resume();
 }
 
+// A file: URL's path in AmigaDOS form. URL::fileSystemPath() is the URL's
+// path with a leading "/", which AmigaDOS reads as the parent directory:
+// - file:///Volume:dir/file (and PROGDIR:, or any assign) is Volume:dir/file;
+// - file:///Volume/dir/file, the Unix form, is Volume:dir/file;
+// - a path of one name (file:///page.html) stays relative: page.html in the
+//   current directory, as before;
+// - dir/file that exists relative to the current directory is read there
+//   (a page under file:///page.html asking for "pages/x.html"), before it is
+//   taken as Volume/file. That check is relative, so it never brings up an
+//   "insert volume" requester.
+static String amigaFileSystemPath(const URL& url)
+{
+    String path = url.fileSystemPath();
+    while (path.startsWith('/'))
+        path = path.substring(1);
+    size_t slash = path.find('/');
+    size_t colon = path.find(':');
+    if (colon != notFound && (slash == notFound || colon < slash))
+        return path;
+    if (slash == notFound || !slash)
+        return path;
+    if (FileSystem::fileExists(path))
+        return path;
+    return makeString(StringView { path }.left(slash), ':', StringView { path }.substring(slash + 1));
+}
+
 // file: URLs: curl is built for http and https only, so files are read here
 // and handed over from the run loop, as a network load would be.
 void ResourceHandle::amigaLoadFile()
@@ -210,12 +236,13 @@ void ResourceHandle::amigaLoadFile()
         auto* client = handle.client();
         if (!client)
             return;
-        auto contents = FileSystem::readEntireFile(url.fileSystemPath());
+        auto path = amigaFileSystemPath(url);
+        auto contents = FileSystem::readEntireFile(path);
         if (!contents) {
             client->didFail(&handle, ResourceError("NSURLErrorDomain"_s, -1100, url, "The file does not exist."_s));
             return;
         }
-        auto mimeType = MIMETypeRegistry::mimeTypeForPath(url.fileSystemPath());
+        auto mimeType = MIMETypeRegistry::mimeTypeForPath(path);
         if (mimeType.isEmpty())
             mimeType = "application/octet-stream"_s;
         ResourceResponse response(URL { url }, String { mimeType }, contents->size(), String());
